✅ Traditional AMQP vs Spring Cloud Stream (quick)
| Point              | Traditional (this file)              | Spring Cloud Stream                      |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| API                | `RabbitTemplate` + `@RabbitListener` | Functions / `StreamBridge` + binders     |
| Queue/Exchange     | You declare beans explicitly         | Often created via binding destination    |
| Best fit           | Monolith / fine AMQP control         | Microservices messaging abstraction      |


❌ Common mistakes
1) Missing `spring-boot-starter-web` while using `@RestController`
2) Sending to queue name only and forgetting exchange + routing key (unless using default exchange)
3) Durable queue but non-persistent messages → messages may still be lost on broker restart
4) Routing key mismatch between producer send and binding
